E1 — longest_k_distinct(s, k) → string

Longest substring containing at most k distinct characters.

('eceba', 2)          -> 'ece'
('aa', 1)             -> 'aa'
('abcadcacacaca', 3)  -> 'cadcacacaca'
('', 2)               -> ''
('abc', 0)            -> ''
('abc', 5)            -> 'abc'

Variation of: longest substring without repeating characters. Same machinery — only the shrink condition changes. You'll need best_start, and while not if. Both cost you last time.